# Build-time configuration for the Vercel deployment.
#
# Vite inlines VITE_* into the bundle, so none of this is secret — it is a public URL that every
# visitor receives in plain JavaScript. That is also why it lives here rather than in Vercel's
# project settings: it needs no privileged access to change, and it is reviewed with the code.
# A variable set in Vercel's project settings still wins over this file.
#
# `vite build` loads this file automatically (mode=production). `pnpm dev` runs mode=development and
# does not, so use .env.local for local work.
#
# One keeper serves every chain, each under its CoW network name: …/keeper/xdai, …/keeper/mainnet,
# …/keeper/base. Deployed by cowprotocol/infrastructure (cow-drop stack, staging). No /v1 suffix.
# To point one chain elsewhere, add VITE_KEEPER_URLS=<chainId>=<url> — it overrides this per chain.
VITE_KEEPER_BASE_URL=https://drop.barn.cow.fi/keeper
